module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_untyped_empty_map_fold_seed_is_emitted_with_a_bare_alias_head

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data an_untyped_empty_map_fold_seed_is_emitted_with_a_bare_alias_head: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_untyped_empty_map_fold_seed_is_emitted_with_a_bare_alias_head" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "E0107 on gunbc#14084: the seed-emitter renders an untyped `empty_map()` in a fold `init` position with the type alias expanded to its bare head: `fold(names, init: empty_map(), f: fn(acc, name) { map_insert(acc, name, qualified_name_snoc(qn: p, segment: name)) })` returning Map<Symbol, QualifiedName> emitted `v1_rt::rc_empty_map::<Symbol, Rc<FreeMonoid>>()`, dropping FreeMonoid's argument (QualifiedName = FreeMonoid<Symbol>); rustc refuses `E0107 missing generics for type alias std_algebra::FreeMonoid` at stage0/src/v2_compiler_resolve.rs:3337 (CI receipts: head d948d9a and e64a435). A typed `let seed: Map<Symbol, QualifiedName> = empty_map()` emitted `rc_empty_map::<_, _>()` and compiled."

    "INVALID STATE: a well-typed .dag fold over an alias-typed map is accepted by the compiler and emitted as Rust that does not compile. HARM: the required emit-and-build job refuses (EmittedCompilerBuildFailed, floor_class=structural) on source the checker admitted, so the author must find a source shape the emitter happens to render; the refusal is loud, not silent."

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable -- the failure is caught only by building the emitted crate. CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed: the emitter renders an inferred type by its full application (alias expanded to FreeMonoid<Symbol>) or by a placeholder, never by the bare head. NEXT TRIGGER: the seed-emitter's type rendering for an inferred generic argument; owner tidy-swift-183 (queued after #14069, per clever-crane-830). WORKAROUND (labeled): src/v2/compiler/resolve.dag type_param_value_binders types its seed with a let; delete that let when the emitter renders the alias correctly."

    "STANDING (2026-10-16): REPRODUCED on main only in the self-host build. With the resolve.dag type_param_value_binders typed-let workaround deleted, //gunbc/instruments:self-host over v2.compiler.source_root_eval refuses E0107 at stage0/src/v2_compiler_resolve.rs:3371 on main's emitter; that is the discriminating RED. Probe on that tree (node dump at the seed's type argument): the argument reference QualifiedName carries children [Symbol] (the application) while child_type_node returns its expansion FreeMonoid with two variant children (Empty, Cons), no arguments. resolved_type's contract is the expansion; the application lives on the reference, so the earliest unjustified link is the emitter reading a type-argument position through the expansion accessor (no upstream writer drops anything). Two sites carried the bare head: the seed turbofish rc_empty_map::<Symbol, Rc<FreeMonoid>>() and the fold lambda's acc annotation Rc<HashMap<Symbol, Rc<FreeMonoid>>>. Fix (05_emit_rust rust_type_argument_node, used by the keyed- and element-collection arms of render_rust_type and the empty-map kv rendering): when the declaration's arity n differs from the expansion's child count and equals the reference's, the application is the reference's children. The typed-let workaround is deleted and the self-host build executes the untyped seed. The four native-emission-controls cases (alias_empty_map_seed_*) are GUARDS, not discriminators: same-module, cross-module, real QualifiedName/Symbol and match-arm shapes all emit and compile on main, so they do not reproduce the self-host-only shape. REMAINING, named follow-up: other child_type_node consumers that render a type argument through the expansion (set element at render_rust_type, the Python and Go emitters, fn-sig tuple rendering) are not changed here; each is the same read and is fixed by the same accessor when it is shown to reach a parametric alias argument.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: E0107 `missing generics for type alias` naming a std alias at a turbofish in an emitted file; the source holds an untyped empty_map()/empty collection in an init or argument position whose element type is an alias of a generic."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
